<h2 id="redflags" class="scroll-mt-24">Red Flags to Watch For</h2>
<ul>
<li>Surgeon pressures you into surgery at the first visit, or refuses a second opinion</li>
<li>No clear diagnosis offered, or a diagnosis given without examination or imaging</li>
<li>No 3D VSP shown for orthognathic cases</li>
<li>No discussion of non-surgical alternatives</li>
<li>No before-and-after portfolio, or only stock-style images</li>
<li>Unusually low cost with no explanation, or a quote that changes after admission</li>
<li>Surgeon not present at the consultation — only a counsellor or "patient manager"</li>
<li>Hospital not equipped with in-house CT, ICU, or a dedicated anaesthesia team</li>
<li>No clear consent process or written plan</li>
<li>Reviews that are all recent, identical in tone, or unverifiable</li>
</ul>
