<h2 id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 font-headline-md text-primary mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="not-prose space-y-4 mb-12">
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">What is the difference between MDS and MCh in maxillofacial surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">MDS is a 3-year dental-surgical postgraduate degree (the standard). MCh is a 3-year surgical superspecialty, usually for surgeons who first did MBBS, MS, or DNB. Both can be excellent maxillofacial surgeons — what matters most is sub-specialty training in your specific procedure.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">How many years of training does a maxillofacial surgeon need?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">At least 3 years of specialist training after dental or medical school, often with additional fellowship. Total: 8–10 years of training from undergraduate, plus years of supervised practice before operating independently on complex cases.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Should I get a second opinion?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Yes — for any major surgery. A good surgeon welcomes a second opinion. If a surgeon discourages it, that is a red flag. A second consultation also lets you compare surgical plans and prices before committing.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Are the cheapest surgeons the best?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Not necessarily. Cost reflects surgeon experience, hospital quality, anaesthesia team, and implant quality. Look for value, not just price. A lower quote that excludes imaging, VSP, anaesthesia, or implant quality is not actually a bargain.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Is hospital choice important?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Yes. The hospital should have ICU support, modern anaesthesia, and an experienced surgical team. Specialised maxillofacial units usually have all of these, and choosing one reduces the risk of last-minute rescheduling or compromised care.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">How do I check a surgeon's credentials?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Verify with the Dental Council of India or National Medical Commission via their online directories. Look at publications on PubMed and Google Scholar. Check AOMSI, IAOMS, and AO Foundation memberships. Cross-check the qualification, registration number, and society affiliations on the surgeon's own website.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Should I travel to Hyderabad for surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Yes, if it means access to a specialist. Most maxillofacial patients travel for the right surgeon, not the nearest one. Hyderabad's connectivity by air, range of recovery-friendly stays, and concentration of maxillofacial specialists make it a sensible destination for jaw, TMJ, and facial trauma work.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Do you offer virtual consultations?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Yes — virtual consultations are available for out-of-town and international patients. They are useful for an initial opinion, review of reports, and treatment planning. The full clinical examination and final surgical plan still require an in-person visit before surgery.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">How much does maxillofacial surgery cost in Hyderabad?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Costs vary by procedure. Single-jaw orthognathic surgery usually ranges from ₹1.5 lakh to ₹3.5 lakh, bimaxillary surgery from ₹2.5 lakh to ₹5.5 lakh, and TMJ arthroscopy is lower. Complex trauma reconstruction and total joint replacement are higher. Always ask what is included — imaging, VSP, anaesthesia, implants, and hospital stay.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Are maxillofacial surgeons in Hyderabad qualified for international patients?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Many are. The best maxillofacial practices in the city are NABH-affiliated, follow international sterilisation and consent protocols, and are accustomed to handling patients from the Gulf, Africa, and South-East Asia. Ask for international patient testimonials, telemedicine options, and pre-arrival documentation support before you book.</p></details>
